      "problem": "$\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{3}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
